  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Every Child Supported Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program will be implemented in Bosnia and Herzegovina, Ukraine and Zambia. Together, Bris, La Strada Ukraine, Lifeline/Childline Zambia and Nova Generacija/Blue Phone aim to counter the degradation of 
children rights in each context of focus and ensure that children have the support they have the 
right to. All organizations involved in this program operate child helplines who support thousands of children 
on a yearly basis. The focus of each project in the program is based on what children talk about 
in the contacts with the child helpline to ensure local relevance. Additionally, the organizations form important part of the civil society in each context of implementation thus are well connected to the target group of people, 
especially children and youth, living in poverty and oppression.</narrative>
  </description>
